  "note": "Triennial election of the Antrim Town Commissioners, polled Wednesday 18 May 1949. Only nine nominations were received for the nine seats, so there was no contest (Ballymena Observer, 27 May 1949, p. 2). Mr. Robert Wright did not seek re-election and the vacancy was filled by Mr. Stewart. Returned unopposed."
